// @error float literal overflows f64
// The exponent participates in the magnitude, so the overflow judgement has to see
// it: `1e400` has ONE integer digit and is still past the f64 range. The checker's
// prescreen shifts the digit count by the exponent before consulting the real
// encoder, so this stays a clean CHECKER rejection instead of falling through to
// the emitter's `emitFail` backstop.
let a = 1e400
print(a)
